            title: 'Seven-Toed Pete Race Horse',
            subtitle: 'Fast Fives Dominoes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Seven-Toed Pete is a fast Fives-family domino game for four players. Players score on multiples of five and gain extra turns whenever they score or play a double.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Seven-Toed Pete is a U.S. Fives-family domino game. The same name has also been used for an unrelated poker game, but this entry covers the domino game only.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Four players in the standard game; some groups also use partnership or 2-3 player variants.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 28-tile double-six set, from 0-0 to 6-6.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Domino set and score tracker (chips or score sheet).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Each player receives 7 tiles; all tiles are dealt, so there is no boneyard.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
